* Peavey 5150 preamp stage 3 of 3: the tone stack with its post pots and V3A.
* V5A's output (o5a) arrives through the link source VLNK, with R89 as in the drawing.
*
* Not modelled: the effects loop (bypassed: send and return joined), the preamp out, the clamp mute, S1C
* (Bright, left open) and the V3B cathode follower that the drawing taps from the stack input (C59 .01u, R94 47k,
* R79, R80, R16) and couples into the post-pot node through C52 .022u: as read, it would pass the stack input
* around the tone controls almost unattenuated and make LOW / MID / HIGH inaudible, so it is left out until the
* drawing can be checked against a real amp.

V VRAIL x3 100 440
V VX2 x2 50 338
S VLNK o5a 40k 0
R R89 o5a tb 470k

* Tone stack input bus tb: 33k to ground.
R R24 tb 0 33k

* Marshall-type stack: 570p to the HIGH pot (VR5, 250k), 47k slope, 0.022u caps, LOW (VR3, 1M rheostat),
* MID (VR4, 50k) with its 0.022u, and the 47k R95 from the LOW/MID junction to ground.
C C14 tb ts 470p
C C60 tb ts 100p
R VR5_T ts w5 1
R VR5_B w5 su 1
R R28 tb sm 47k
C C18 sm su 22n
R VR3 su sv 1
R VR4_T sv w4 1
R VR4_B w4 0 1
C C21 sm w4 22n
R R95 sv 0 47k

* Post pots: VR6 (clean) and VR7 (ultra) on the stack output; K2B takes one of them to node m.
R VR6_T w5 w6 1
R VR6_B w6 0 1
R VR7_T w5 w7 1
R VR7_B w7 0 1
R SW_K2B6 w6 m 1
R SW_K2B5 w7 m 1e12
R R81 m 0 2M2


* V3A: 0.047u from m, 1M and 220k grid leaks; plate 68k, cathode 3.3k with 4.7n. Its plate is the
* output (node pl, after the 0.022u coupling cap C49 with the 1M of the inverter's input network).
C C11 m g3a 47n
R R26 g3a 0 1M
R R85 g3a 0 220k
T V3A g3a p3a k3a ECC83
R R5 x2 p3a 68k
R R14 k3a 0 3k3
C C61 k3a 0 4n7
C C49L p3a pl 22n
R RPIL pl 0 1M
